---
import BaseLayout from "@layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { createPageSeo } from "@lib/seo/seo-config";
import { createBreadcrumbs } from "@lib/breadcrumbs/breadcrumbs";
import { breadcrumbListSchema, faqSchema } from "@lib/schema/schema";
import { canonicalUrl } from "@lib/urls/url-utils";
import { siteBrand, siteContact } from "@data/site/site-config";
import { pricingPlans, pricingNote, usdPrice } from "@data/pricing/plans";
import { usd } from "@data/countries/international";

// ---------- FAQ (visible list and FAQPage schema share this array) ----------

const faqs = [
  {
    question: "Is BtechWaleTech an Australian web development company?",
    answer: "No, and we will not pretend to be. We are a small team of engineers based in India who build websites, ecommerce stores, SEO systems, custom software and AI automations for Australian businesses, working remotely. We have no Australian office, no ABN and no local address. You deal directly with the engineers who plan and build your project.",
  },
  {
    question: "How much does a website cost for an Australian business?",
    answer: `With us, a static website of up to 100 pages starts from ${usd("Static")}, a 700+ page SEO website from ${usd("SEO website")}, AI automation from ${usd("AI automation")}, an ecommerce store from ${usd("Ecommerce")} and a custom web app from ${usd("Custom web app")}. Monthly SEO starts from ${usd("Monthly SEO")} and maintenance from ${usd("Maintenance")}. These are starting prices in US dollars; the final quote depends on your requirements.`,
  },
  {
    question: "Can you invoice in Australian dollars?",
    answer: "Yes, on request. We quote in US dollars by default and can issue the invoice in AUD at the rate on the day of the quote. Most Australian clients pay through Wise, which lets you pay with an ordinary local bank transfer, or by international wire. Payments are split into milestones and nothing is due before you approve a written scope.",
  },
  {
    question: "Do your prices include Australian GST?",
    answer: "Our starting prices are quoted in US dollars and do not include Australian GST. We are an overseas supplier, so how an imported service is treated in your books, including any reverse-charge question, is for your accountant to confirm. We can put whatever business details you need on the invoice.",
  },
  {
    question: "How does the time difference between India and Australia work?",
    answer: "Australia is ahead of India all year: 2.5 hours in Perth, 4 to 5 hours in Adelaide and Darwin, and 4.5 to 5.5 hours on the east coast depending on daylight saving. Our morning in India lines up with your afternoon, so calls usually happen between about 1pm and 5pm on the east coast and late morning in Perth. Work continues through our day, so feedback sent in your afternoon is often actioned by your next morning.",
  },
  {
    question: "Which Australian cities and states do you work with?",
    answer: "All of them, remotely: Sydney and the rest of New South Wales, Melbourne and Victoria, Brisbane, the Gold Coast and Queensland, Perth and Western Australia, Adelaide and South Australia, Canberra, Hobart and Tasmania, and Darwin in the Northern Territory. Regional businesses get the same process and prices as capital-city ones.",
  },
  {
    question: "Can you set up Afterpay, Zip, Stripe or PayPal on our store?",
    answer: "Yes. We connect the payment options you choose, such as Stripe, Shopify Payments, PayPal or Square for cards and wallets, and buy now pay later providers such as Afterpay or Zip where your platform supports them and the provider approves your merchant application. Merchant accounts are opened in your business name, never ours.",
  },
  {
    question: "Can you help us rank on google.com.au?",
    answer: "We handle the parts of SEO that are within our control: technical health, site structure, speed, on-page content written for Australian searches, LocalBusiness schema, internal linking and hreflang when you run separate Australian and New Zealand pages. We also guide you through your Google Business Profile, which must be verified by you. Nobody can guarantee rankings, so we report what changed and what moved.",
  },
  {
    question: "Will our website follow the Privacy Act and the Spam Act?",
    answer: "We build with the Australian Privacy Principles and the Spam Act in mind: a clear privacy policy page, collection notices on forms, unticked consent boxes, working unsubscribe links and minimal data collection. We are engineers, not lawyers, so we do not give legal advice or certify compliance. Please have your adviser review the policy wording and confirm which obligations apply to your business.",
  },
  {
    question: "Do you build accessible websites to WCAG standards?",
    answer: "Yes. We build to WCAG 2.2 level AA as a working target: semantic headings, keyboard navigation, visible focus states, labelled form fields, sufficient colour contrast, captions where you supply them and alt text on meaningful images. Accessibility also matters under the Disability Discrimination Act. We test with automated tools and manual keyboard checks, but we do not issue formal certification.",
  },
  {
    question: "Can you register our .com.au domain?",
    answer: "A .com.au or .au domain has to be registered by an entity with an Australian presence, such as a business with an ABN, so you register it in your name with an Australian registrar and give us DNS access. We then connect it to hosting, set up SSL and email records, and document everything. The domain always stays yours.",
  },
  {
    question: "Where will our website be hosted?",
    answer: "Wherever suits the project. Static sites usually go on a global CDN with edge locations in Australia, which keeps pages fast in Perth and Sydney alike. Apps with a database can run in an Australian cloud region, such as the Sydney or Melbourne regions offered by major cloud providers, where data location or speed matters. Hosting accounts are opened in your name.",
  },
  {
    question: "Do you work with tradies and NDIS providers?",
    answer: "Yes. For trades we build fast mobile sites with click-to-call, suburb service-area pages and quote forms, and can connect enquiries to job management software. For NDIS providers we build clear service pages, accessible layouts and careful enquiry forms. We do not claim NDIS registration expertise; your registration details and wording should come from you.",
  },
  {
    question: "Can you connect our website to Xero, MYOB, ServiceM8 or Cliniko?",
    answer: `Usually, yes. These tools have APIs or integration platforms, so enquiries, bookings, invoices and customer records can flow between your website and the software you already use. We map your current workflow first, then scope the automation. AI automation starts from ${usd("AI automation")}.`,
  },
  {
    question: "Who owns the website and code after launch?",
    answer: "You do. Source code, content, design files, the hosting account, the domain and every admin login are handed over in accounts under your name. We keep no licence over your build and no credentials you cannot change.",
  },
  {
    question: "Is maintenance really free for five months?",
    answer: `Yes. Once hosting goes live, five months of maintenance are included: content updates, bug fixes, security updates, backups, and uptime and speed checks. After that you can continue from ${usd("Maintenance")} or contact us only when you need a change.`,
  },
  {
    question: "How long does a website project take?",
    answer: "A static website usually takes one to two weeks, a 700+ page SEO website three to five weeks, AI automation two to four weeks, an ecommerce store four to eight weeks and a custom web app six to twelve weeks. Content and approvals arriving on time matter more than anything else, including the time difference.",
  },
  {
    question: "Can you redesign our existing site without losing Google rankings?",
    answer: "Yes. Before the redesign we export the pages that get search traffic, keep their URLs where possible, set up 301 redirects where URLs must change, carry over titles and content that rank, and watch Search Console after launch. Most ranking losses after a rebuild come from skipping those steps.",
  },
  {
    question: "Can we meet in person?",
    answer: "No. We are a remote team in India and do not have staff in Australia. Everything runs over video calls, WhatsApp, email and a shared staging link, with written scopes and updates, so you always have a record of what was agreed.",
  },
  {
    question: "How do we get started?",
    answer: "Send a WhatsApp message or an email with what your business does, what you want built and a few sites you like. We reply with questions, then a written scope, timeline and itemised quote, usually within two working days. Work starts after you approve the scope and pay the first milestone.",
  },
