      "We are engineers, not lawyers or accountants, and nothing on this page is legal or tax advice. What follows is the practical groundwork we build into Australian websites so that your adviser has less to fix. Please have a qualified professional confirm which obligations apply to your business and approve any policy wording.",
      "<strong>Privacy Act 1988 and the Australian Privacy Principles.</strong> The thirteen APPs cover how organisations collect, use, disclose, store and give access to personal information. They apply to Australian Government agencies and to businesses above the turnover threshold, and also to some smaller businesses, including health service providers and businesses that trade in personal information. The Act has been amended in recent years and further reform has been under active discussion, so check the current position with your adviser rather than relying on an old template. Whether or not the Act strictly applies to you, we build as if it does: a real privacy policy, a collection notice next to each form explaining what is collected and why, only the fields you actually need, and form data stored in access-controlled systems.",
      "<strong>Cross-border disclosure and working with us.</strong> Because our team is in India, it is worth thinking about APP 8, which deals with disclosing personal information overseas. The simplest approach is the one we use by default: we build and test with dummy data on staging, customer data lives in your systems or your hosting accounts, and we only access live personal information when a task genuinely needs it and you have agreed. If your adviser wants specific contractual terms about data handling, we are happy to sign them.",
      "<strong>Notifiable data breaches.</strong> Organisations covered by the Privacy Act must notify affected people and the Office of the Australian Information Commissioner about eligible data breaches. Good engineering reduces the chance of a breach in the first place: HTTPS everywhere, patched software, least-privilege accounts, two-factor authentication on admin logins, backups that are tested, and no personal data sitting in email inboxes or open spreadsheets.",
      "<strong>Spam Act 2003.</strong> Commercial emails and SMS messages need consent, must identify the sender, and must include a functional unsubscribe option that is honoured promptly. We build newsletter and marketing sign-ups with unticked consent boxes and clear wording, connect them to tools that handle unsubscribes automatically, and keep a record of how and when each person opted in. The Australian Communications and Media Authority enforces these rules and has issued significant penalties.",
      "<strong>Australian Consumer Law.</strong> The ACL prohibits misleading or deceptive conduct, requires consumer guarantees that cannot be excluded, and requires a single total price to be shown where a price is quoted. Unfair contract terms in standard form contracts can now attract penalties. For websites this affects pricing displays, returns pages, testimonials, comparison claims, subscription sign-ups and terms and conditions. We build honest defaults and you confirm the wording.",
      "<strong>Accessibility, WCAG and the Disability Discrimination Act.</strong> The Disability Discrimination Act 1992 applies to goods and services, including websites, and the Australian Human Rights Commission's guidance points to the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines. The well-known Maguire v SOCOG case over the Sydney 2000 Olympics website showed that inaccessible websites can lead to real legal consequences. We build to WCAG 2.2 level AA as a working target: semantic headings, keyboard access, focus states, labelled fields, colour contrast, text alternatives and forms that announce errors clearly. Government and many funded organisations have their own formal requirements, which we follow when you share them.",
      "<strong>GST.</strong> GST in Australia is 10 per cent, and businesses must register once their GST turnover reaches the registration threshold. For your website, that means GST-inclusive consumer prices, correct tax invoices and correct tax settings in your store and accounting software. For your purchase from us, we quote in US dollars without Australian GST, and your accountant should confirm how an imported service is treated for your business.",
